{"version":"0.1.0","date":"2026-04-19","summary":"Create first complete skill-auditor design spec and repository control files.","rationale":"The project starts in spec-first mode. The canonical design, implementation tracker, revision log, reference analysis, and README must exist before implementation begins.","spec_refs":["Problem and Goal","Scope and Non-Goals","Core Decisions","Data and Interface Contracts","Implementation Phases or Rollout Steps"],"checklist_ids":["repo-controls"]}
{"version":"0.1.1","date":"2026-04-19","summary":"Move the canonical spec package under docs/spec and align the repository top-level structure.","rationale":"The project should expose docs, skills, hooks, and README.md at the repository root. The previous root-level spec files were a packaging mistake, not a product requirement.","spec_refs":["Problem and Goal","Ownership or Source of Truth","Core Decisions","Data and Interface Contracts"],"checklist_ids":["repo-controls"]}
{"version":"0.1.2","date":"2026-04-19","summary":"Separate shared audit design from ecosystem-specific deltas and make global audit host-aware by default.","rationale":"Common logic should stay unified, but Codex and Claude Code differences must be called out explicitly. Default global audit scope should follow the current host ecosystem and only scan both ecosystems under explicit override.","spec_refs":["Scope and Non-Goals","Core Decisions","System Boundaries","Data and Interface Contracts","Failure Cases and Acceptance","Implementation Phases or Rollout Steps"],"checklist_ids":["discovery-and-parse","state-and-reporting"]}
{"version":"0.1.3","date":"2026-04-19","summary":"Add hard security and privacy constraints for both audited skills and the audit package itself.","rationale":"Secrets, private data, and suspicious shell or binary execution patterns must be treated as error-level findings, not soft style warnings.","spec_refs":["Core Decisions","Data and Interface Contracts","Failure Cases and Acceptance","Implementation Phases or Rollout Steps"],"checklist_ids":["discovery-and-parse","security-and-shell-safety"]}
{"version":"0.1.4","date":"2026-04-19","summary":"Require the auditor to work directly inside Codex and Claude Code without separate external API configuration.","rationale":"The product should be host-native. External API keys, external model endpoints, and standalone audit services are not part of the required usage model.","spec_refs":["Core Decisions","Data and Interface Contracts","Failure Cases and Acceptance","Implementation Phases or Rollout Steps"],"checklist_ids":["state-and-reporting","overlap-and-active-set","host-native-usage"]}
{"version":"0.1.5","date":"2026-04-19","summary":"Clarify HOST_ECOSYSTEM_UNKNOWN error semantics, add --active-set-max CLI flag, define watch entry point and process lifecycle, define ledger write semantics and prune conditions, and fix update_history to JSON Lines format.","rationale":"Code review identified five ambiguities: HOST_ECOSYSTEM_UNKNOWN lacked user-facing guidance; --active-set-max had no CLI surface; watch process lifecycle (startup, shutdown, concurrency) was unspecified; ledger note/change_log write semantics and prune triggers were undefined; update_history allowed multiple serialization formats creating append inconsistency risk.","spec_refs":["Data and Interface Contracts","Runtime Flows","Ownership or Source of Truth","Deletion and retention semantics"],"checklist_ids":["discovery-and-parse","watch-and-hooks","state-and-reporting","overlap-and-active-set"]}
